 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A drug is a substance that changes how the body or mind works. Drug abuse is using a drug in a harmful way or without a doctor's advice.\nAlcohol is found in beer, wine, spirits and local drinks (palm wine, kwacha, sha, odontol). It slows down the brain and nerves.\nHealth effects: poor judgement and slow reactions (road accidents), vomiting, liver damage (cirrhosis), stomach ulcers, high blood pressure, brain damage, addiction; in pregnancy it harms the baby.\nSocial effects: fights and violence at home, money wasted, poor school work and dropping out, crime, unsafe sex, loss of respect and jobs.\nThe sale of alcohol to young people is forbidden. Young people should refuse it and choose friends who do not drink.",
  "checks": []
 },
